/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  chemistry/H3His-formation.dat -- the first 2 protonations of L-histidine, written from the master:
      HHis + 2 H+  <=>  H3His
  Made by bin/curate/species_c373.py from data/curation/batches/species_c373/*.tsv.

  logK25 and dH are the PRINTED values of the sources below (standard state ideal solution at 1 mol/kg, 298.15 K):
      pK1 = 1.54, dH1 = 3.6 kJ/mol (grade DBA)
      pK2 = 6.07, dH2 = 29.5 kJ/mol, dCp 176 J/mol/K (grade BCA)
      pK3 = 9.34, dH3 = 43.8 kJ/mol, dCp -233 J/mol/K (grade CBA)
  Source: Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231; standard state: hypothetical ideal solution of unit molality, 298.15 K, 0.1 MPa (Section 8, p. 359).
  The master is HHis, the form a case declares; this record carries steps 1 to 2 (the sign flips with the direction written).
  The constant-dCp term of the printed dCp is NOT carried: the record grammar has no place for it (a
  van't Hoff integral with a constant dCp is exactly the `analytic` A1, A3, A4 terms; proposed, not done).
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType aqueousSpeciation;
schemaVersion 1;

species H3His; masters ( { ion HHis; nu 1; } { ion H; nu 2; } );
      logK25 7.61; dH -33100; source "Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231 -- Section 8 summary, p. 360, and Section 7.39, p. 296: pK1 1.54, dH1 3.6 kJ/mol, pK2 6.07, dH2 29.5 kJ/mol (pK, dH_ion at 298.15 K)";
